        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: फलम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फलम् (phalam) — \"fruit (and the result of anything)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फलम् is the fruit on the tree. It is also, in the same breath and with no metaphor felt, the fruit of an action — the result, the reward, the yield. A Sanskrit sentence about the phalam of your work is not reaching for a poetic image; it has one word where English has two."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The root behind it means \"to burst, to bear fruit\", which is the fruit split open at the moment it is ripe. Neuter -अम्, like जलम् (jalam) and अन्नम् before it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word that carries an orchard and a consequence at once."
            }
          ]
        },
