              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपः (dīpaḥ) — \"a lamp\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीपः (dīpaḥ) is a lamp — the small clay one with oil and a wick. Its root means \"to blaze\", so the word names the burning rather than the vessel."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put दीप together with a word meaning \"a row\" and you get dīpāvalī, \"a row of lamps\" — the festival English writes as Diwali. Masculine -अः, like ओदनः (odanaḥ)."
            }
          ]
        },
